# Line endings for every checkout, whatever the local core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, so a Windows clone with Git's default
# core.autocrlf=true still passes the format checks (Prettier and CSharpier expect LF). Git
# detects text and binary files itself; the binary types below are listed so it never guesses.
# The tree holds no file that must be CRLF; a Windows-only script that needs CRLF (.bat, .cmd)
# gets its own line here.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.br binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pfx binary
*.p12 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
